{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q209222","formula":"C₈H₆Cl₂O₃","hill":"C8H6Cl2O3","elements":["H","C","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":8.0,"H":6.0,"O":3.0,"Cl":2.0},"names":{"en":"2,4-dichlorophenoxyacetic acid","ru":"2,4-Дихлорфеноксиуксусная кислота"},"descriptions":{"en":"2,4-Dichlorophenoxyacetic acid is an organic compound with the chemical formula C8H6Cl2O3. It is usually referred to by its ISO common name 2,4-D. It is a systemic herbicide that kills most broadleaf weeds by causing uncontrolled growth, but most grasses such as cereals, lawn turf, and grassland are relatively unaffected. 2,4-D is one of the oldest and most widely available herbicides and defoliants in the world, having been commercially available since 1945, and is now produced by many chemical companies since the patent on it has long since expired.","ru":"2,4-Дихлорфеноксиу́ксусная кислота́ (сокращённо 2,4-Д) — производное феноксиуксусной кислоты, гербицид из группы синтетических ауксинов. Он был разработан American Chemical Paint Co. в 1945 году и структурно связан с дихлорпропом."},"fame":32,"pubchemCid":1486,"mass":221.03,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=CC(=C(C=C1Cl)Cl)OCC(=O)O","inchikey":"OVSKIKFHRZPJSS-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(2,4-dichlorophenoxy)acetic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"1486","atoms":19,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.134,"y":-2.581,"z":0.095,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-4.623,"y":0.365,"z":0.528,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.11,"y":0.035,"z":-0.707,"el":"O"},{"x":4.177,"y":0.972,"z":0.899,"el":"O"},{"x":3.651,"y":-0.871,"z":-0.333,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.221,"y":0.089,"z":-0.416,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.924,"y":-1.052,"z":-0.03,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.879,"y":1.315,"z":-0.51,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.285,"y":-0.967,"z":0.263,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.24,"y":1.4,"z":-0.217,"el":"C"},{"x":1.979,"y":0.841,"z":0.086,"el"